lines+=sect(3,'Actual curricular boundary','The nine core selections include AD determinants, C/I/G/NX channels, price-level movement versus shifts, sticky wages/prices and misperceptions, SRAS/LRAS, potential output and gaps, demand/supply shocks and self-correction. Fiscal work includes purchases, taxes, transfers, spending and tax multipliers, MPC, crowding-out offsets, automatic stabilization, policy lags, uncertainty and demand-versus-supply tradeoffs.','Existing exchange-rate/foreign-income and import-leakage applications remain selected; they do not authorize a new Open Economy audit. Monetary mechanisms and loanable-funds mechanics are protected by prior work; supplied changes in investment or AD can enter integration questions. The five Phillips concepts are selected but explicitly deferred. No separate rules-versus-discretion or detailed policy-institution bank was inferred as a missing objective.')
lines+=sect(4,'Both prior-audit overlap masks','`money-banking-inflation` contains 818 previously audited records across 13 modules; `macro-saving-investment-budgets-debt` contains 268 across seven. This preset shares **zero authoritative IDs with either audit**. All 20 prior definitions match the completed prior snapshots and remain identical in the final library. Independent hashes also guard both prior artifact directories. No reserve/tool/loanable-funds machinery was rebuilt. See `overlap-mask.json` and `architecture-validation.json`.')
lines+=sect(5,'Before/after accounting','Every one of the 728 IDs has a mutually exclusive disposition in `record-actions.json`. Content changes take precedence over accessibility/path changes; accessibility-only means changed evidence without content; path-only means the image reference alone changed. The 47 image-reference corrections comprise 42 path-only and five accompanying content revisions.')
